{
  "id": "ss.terrain.tunnel",
  "name": "Tunnel mouth (SS)",
  "description": "Shape Survivors set dressing: a hole dug up through the field from below, and the same hole caved in. The spoil is heaped highest on the near lip where it was pushed out, and it is warm turned earth rather than the ruins' purple stone — the one ring on this ground that means dug, not built. Drawn at the crater tilt the pheromone vent uses, so a mouth cut into open flats and one cut into a burrow chamber read as the same object. The `filled` variant is what a spent tunnel leaves: the heap gone back down the hole, domed and paler than the ground it came out of, broken into clods on top and sunk away from the lip where it settled.",
  "tags": ["ss-terrain"],
  "size": [76, 44],
  "meta": { "radiusX": 26, "radiusY": 12 },
