  "variants": {
    "filled": {
      "description": "Spent: the tunnel caved in. What blocks it is not a lid over the hole and not one lump either — it is a heap of loose spoil packed right out to the lip and piled past it, seven courses of clods narrowing as they climb, the big ones bedded in the crater and small pale pieces perched on the crest. A course is one seeded scatter drawn three times at that seed, so every clod carries its own rim, body and crown for three parts rather than thirty; each course is sparse enough to keep those rims, stepped far enough apart in y that it cannot climb over the one behind and bury it, and drawn over that one so its rims cut into it — which is what stacks them instead of laying them side by side. Angular rather than round, because earth breaks and does not bubble. The ring survives into this state on purpose: the digging happened, and filling it in does not put the ground back.",
      "remove": ["throat", "dark"],
